-- title:
--   Frobenius twists of isomorphisms between perfect closures
-- statement:
--   Let $k$, $K$, $l$, $L$ be fields, with $K$ an algebra over $k$ and $L$ an algebra over $l$, and assume that $l$ is algebraically closed. Let $q$ be the exponential characteristic of $L$ ($q=1$ if $L$ has characteristic $0$, and $q=p$ if it has characteristic $p>0$). Write $K^{\mathrm{perf}}$ and $L^{\mathrm{perf}}$ for the perfect closures of $K$ and $L$ inside fixed algebraic closures, and let $\mathrm{Isom}_{k,l}(K^{\mathrm{perf}},L^{\mathrm{perf}})$ be the set of ring isomorphisms $\alpha:K^{\mathrm{perf}}\to L^{\mathrm{perf}}$ that carry the image of $k$ onto the image of $l$.
--
--   1. **Frobenius twist.** For $n\in\mathbb N$ and $\alpha\in\mathrm{Isom}_{k,l}(K^{\mathrm{perf}},L^{\mathrm{perf}})$, the twist $\mathrm{Fr}_q^n\alpha$ is $\alpha$ followed by the $n$-th iterate of the Frobenius automorphism of the perfect field $L^{\mathrm{perf}}$:
--   $$
--   (\mathrm{Fr}_q^n\alpha)(x)=\alpha(x)^{q^n}\qquad(x\in K^{\mathrm{perf}}).
--   $$
--   It is again an element of $\mathrm{Isom}_{k,l}(K^{\mathrm{perf}},L^{\mathrm{perf}})$: it is a ring isomorphism, and it still maps the image of $k$ onto the image of $l$ because every element of the algebraically closed field $l$ is a $q^n$-th power.
--
--   Frobenius twists are invisible to absolute Galois groups, so a field isomorphism can only be reconstructed from Galois data up to such twists. The equivalence relation generated by single Frobenius steps $\beta(x)=\alpha(x)^p$ relates $\alpha$ to every twist $\mathrm{Fr}_q^n\alpha$; hence two isomorphisms $\alpha,\beta$ are equivalent as soon as $\mathrm{Fr}_q^m\alpha=\mathrm{Fr}_q^n\beta$ for some $m,n\in\mathbb N$, and this is the form in which the injectivity argument concludes.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The twist is `frobeniusPerfectIsom q n α`, with hypotheses `[ExpChar L q]` and `[IsAlgClosed l]`; its defining formula is the simp lemma `frobeniusPerfectIsom_apply`. The set $\mathrm{Isom}_{k,l}(K^{\mathrm{perf}},L^{\mathrm{perf}})$ is `PerfectIsom k K l L`. In characteristic $0$ one has $q=1$ and the twist is $\alpha$ itself.
